  "goodToKnow": "Das Freihandelsabkommen is a free trade agreement: CETA (EU–Canada), the EU–Mercosur deal. In 2015–16, hundreds of thousands protested in Germany against TTIP, the planned EU–US agreement, which was later shelved; chlorine chicken (Chlorhühnchen) became the symbol of fears about food standards. Germany, as an export nation, generally supports free trade. Das Abkommen means agreement. Plural: die Freihandelsabkommen."
